Networking Basics – TCP, UDP & Application Services


## 📦 Transport Layer (Layer 4)
Responsible for:
- End-to-end communication
- Segmentation & reassembly
- Error detection
- Flow control


## 🔵 TCP (Transmission Control Protocol)

### ✅ Features
- Connection-oriented
- Reliable
- Ordered delivery
- Error recovery
- Flow control

### 🔁 3-Way Handshake
1. SYN
2. SYN-ACK
3. ACK

###  Characteristics
- Slower
- Uses sequence numbers
- Retransmits lost packets

###  Use Cases
- HTTP / HTTPS
- FTP
- SMTP, IMAP, POP3
- SSH

---

##  UDP (User Datagram Protocol)

###  Features
- Connectionless
- No reliability
- No ordering
- No retransmission

###  Characteristics
- Faster
- Low overhead
- No handshake

###  Use Cases
- Streaming (video/audio)
- Online gaming
- VoIP
- DNS

---

##  TCP vs UDP

| Feature     | TCP            | UDP            |
|------------|---------------|---------------|
| Connection | Yes           | No            |
| Reliability| High          | Low           |
| Speed      | Slower        | Faster        |
| Ordering   | Yes           | No            |

---

##  Port Numbers

###  Range
0 – 65535

### Types

#### Well-Known Ports (0–1023)
| Port | Protocol |
|------|---------|
| 80   | HTTP    |
| 443  | HTTPS   |
| 21   | FTP     |
| 22   | SSH     |
| 25   | SMTP    |
| 53   | DNS     |

#### Registered Ports (1024–49151)
- Used by applications

#### Dynamic Ports (49152–65535)
- Temporary (client-side)

---

##  Application Layer Services

### Role
- Interface between user and network
- Provides services to applications

---

### Common Protocols

####  HTTP / HTTPS
- Web communication
- HTTPS = Secure

####  Email
- SMTP → Send
- POP3 → Download
- IMAP → Sync

####  FTP
- File transfer

####  DNS
- Domain → IP resolution

####  DHCP
- Automatic IP assignment

---

##  TCP/IP Model

| Layer           | Protocols        |
|----------------|------------------|
| Application    | HTTP, FTP, DNS   |
| Transport      | TCP, UDP         |
| Internet       | IP               |
| Network Access | Ethernet         |

---

##  Key Points

- TCP = Reliable, slower
- UDP = Fast, unreliable
- Ports identify services
- Application layer = user interaction

---

##  Quick Tips

- Reliability needed → TCP
- Speed needed → UDP
- HTTP → Port 80
- HTTPS → Port 443
- DNS → UDP
